# The fixes of the review of step 25, the reasoning part: what the
# interface keeps of a reasoning, and where the viewer reads the rest from
# (docs/steps/step-25-fixes/parts/reasoning.md).

[break] reasoning-copied-into-its-summary
rule: A finished reasoning's words are moved from its stream to the block it draws, not copied: one copy is held.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app/items.rs
in: finish_reasoning
find: let mut text = std::mem::take(&mut reasoning.text);
replace: let mut text = reasoning.text.clone();
caught-by:
    cineris-tui::it memory::a_finished_reasoning_is_held_once_in_each_presenter
    cineris-tui app::items::tests::each_reasoning_knows_its_run_of_its_item_and_holds_its_words_once

[break] reasoning-kept-without-a-bound
rule: A kept reasoning holds its words to their first REASONING_KEPT bytes.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/transcript/kept.rs
in: bound_reasoning
find: if words.len() <= REASONING_KEPT {
replace: if words.len() <= usize::MAX {
