[break] reasoning-runs-not-ended-by-a-call
rule: A tool call between two reasoning parts ends the first run, as its delta ends the block.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app/items.rs
in: edge
find: Shape::Call => Edge::Ends,
replace: Shape::Call => Edge::Nothing,
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::items::tests::each_reasoning_knows_its_run_of_its_item_and_holds_its_words_once

[break] a-reset-response-keeps-its-reasoning-findable
rule: A response thrown away and tried again leaves the reasoning it drew findable by no read.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app/items.rs
in: Mapper::reset
find: reasoning.origin = None;
replace: let _ = &reasoning.origin;
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::items::tests::each_reasoning_knows_its_run_of_its_item_and_holds_its_words_once

[break] a-cut-reasoning-shows-what-was-kept
rule: Enter on a reasoning kept only in part reads it whole from its item.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/transcript/kept.rs
in: Kept::summary
find: Some(origin) if reasoning.cut => Some(Summary::ReadReasoning(origin.clone())),
replace: Some(origin) if reasoning.cut && origin.run == usize::MAX => Some(Summary::ReadReasoning(origin.clone())),
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::tests::screen::a_reasoning_kept_only_in_part_is_read_whole_from_its_item
    cineris-tui transcript::tests::a_kept_reasoning_holds_its_words_once_to_their_bound

